The test suite is strongest on engine equivalence and graph/eager identity, but it mostly compares optimized code to its own reference implementation; it does not independently validate mctx semantics. It also contains a deliberately vacuous continuous-bookkeeping assertion (`... or True`) and a solver test narrow enough that the state-leak risk needs a direct adversarial check. Next I’m cross-referencing the research assumptions and run artifacts.
